  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "iJ93s01L1FMX0cObOna3OO92qGM=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:31.954Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "BEC Financial Technologies is a member-owned cooperative whose owners include Nykredit and Arbejdernes Landsbank. The ownership structure is the claim: the customers and the shareholders are the same Danish banks.\n\nThat changes what a technology decision is. In a normal vendor relationship a supplier persuades a buyer; in a cooperative the buyers collectively own the supplier, so adopting something new is a decision the owner-banks take about their own shared infrastructure. It is slower and harder to reach from outside, and it also means a decision, once taken, lands across every member at once.\n\nNothing about its stack or open-source posture was researched, so the lead is qualified on structure alone and sits at priority 4 pending that screen. It is one of several Danish cooperatives in this set, and the recurrence of the structure is itself the pattern worth noting.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- BEC Financial Technologies (DK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> MEMBER-OWNED COOPERATIVE. Owners include Nykredit and Arbejdernes Landsbank.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:31.954915Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:31.954919Z"
    }
  },
